Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator
and subsequent owner(s) (each and all, an "owner") of an original work of
authorship and/or a database (each, a "Work").

Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights to a Work for
the purpose of contributing to a commons of creative, cultural and
scientific works ("Commons") that the public can reliably and without fear
of later liability claims build upon. The owner that contributes to a Commons
under this document intends that contributions be considered part of the
Commons, freely available for use by anyone for any purpose without restriction
under copyright law. Contributors are not expected to relinquish any other
rights (including trademark and patent rights), nor do contributors expect
to waive moral rights (such as attribution and integrity) to the extent they
are recognized under applicable law.

Accordingly, to the extent possible under applicable law, the contributor who
chooses to dedicate a Work under this document (each, an "Affirmer") hereby:
- waives all Copyright and Related Rights in the Work worldwide;
- dedicates the Work to the public domain to the maximum extent permitted by
  applicable law;
- grants everyone a royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use the Work for any
  purpose; and
- agrees not to assert any claims against anyone exercising such rights.

This document is not intended to displace any applicable law that may provide
greater freedom to the public than this document does.

